SUMMARY:Exercise Horizon 2026 - Family / Friend (arrive 11:00)
LOCATION:Forster Park Community Centre\, Forster Park\, Belmont WA 6104
DESCRIPTION:Your reporting time for Exercise Horizon 2026 is confirmed.\n\n
 FAMILY / FRIEND - ARRIVE 11:00 AWST\nReport to Forster Park Community Cent
 re\, Forster Park\, Belmont WA 6104.\n\nYou represent the loved ones arriv
 ing at the airport for news of someone on the aircraft\, which is what put
 s the reunification process to the test. You do not go to the airfield.\n\
 nPARKING\nBelmont Sports & Recreation Club\, 400 Abernethy Rd\, Cloverdale
  WA 6105.\nParking location: https://maps.app.goo.gl/FGvVXhEoM1re1Fv18\nTh
 en walk north across Abernethy Road to Forster Park. The walking route is 
 attached to this invitation\, and is also at:\nhttps://nicholaspagonis.git
 hub.io/Exercise-Horizon-2026/assets/parking-map.jpg\n\nHOW THE DAY RUNS\nA
 rrive at Forster Park and check in with the Volunteer Coordinators for you
 r briefing.\nYou are issued a red family/friend card carrying the details 
 you need to complete the match.\nYou then wait at the Survivor Reception f
 or your matched passenger to be discharged and bussed back from the incide
 nt site.\nLunch is provided at Forster Park.\nThe exercise finishes at 14:
 00.\n\nEach Family / Friend is matched to exactly one Patient and Passenge
 r\, so both halves need to attend. Tell the Emergency Operations team as e
 arly as possible if your availability changes.\n\nBRING: enclosed footwear
 \, a reusable water bottle\, and any personal medication you may need.\n\n
 Full details and role descriptions: https://nicholaspagonis.github.io/Exer
 cise-Horizon-2026\nQuestions: Emergency.Exercise@perthairport.com.au or 04
 39 237 973
